  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Dehydroascorbic acid may interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Dehydroascorbic acid to the sodium-dependent noradrenaline transporter, which is subsequently targeted by a complex compound with high specificity for the kinase CDC2L1. The second pathway connects Dehydroascorbic acid to glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase, which is targeted by another compound that also acts on CDC2L1. The third pathway shows Dehydroascorbic acid targeting glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase, which is then targeted by a different compound that also acts on the same kinase. These findings collectively indicate that Dehydroascorbic acid may influence the activity of CDC2L1 through different molecular intermediates, suggesting a potential role in regulatory processes involving the kinase. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, but the strength of the relationships varies, with the first pathway showing the highest confidence. The mechanisms involve target-mediated interactions, highlighting the importance of these intermediates in the overall regulatory network.",
